      "id": 1,
      "text": "Embarcadero’s foundations were laid with rubble from the 1906 earthquake and subsequent fires.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://sanfrancisco.wiki/a/Embarcadero"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The first segment of the Embarcadero Freeway opened in 1959, linking the Bay Bridge to Broadway.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/California_State_Route_480"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The 1989 Loma Prieta earthquake damaged the Embarcadero Freeway, prompting its removal in 1991.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16,
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.foundsf.org/The_Embarcadero_Reborn"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Today the new Embarcadero boulevard features bicycle lanes and a dedicated right‑of‑way for the F Market & Wharves streetcar.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.foundsf.org/The_Embarcadero_Reborn"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Ferry Building Marketplace, a historic landmark, anchors the waterfront and serves as a culinary hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
